&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem-Solve Creatively:&lt;/strong&gt; Approach customer challenges with curiosity and creativity—meeting them where they are today while guiding them toward scalable, future-forward direct mail strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will you bring to this role…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Sales Success:&lt;/strong&gt; 3+ years of B2B SaaS closing experience, with a track record of consistently meeting or exceeding quota.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Account Planning&lt;/strong&gt;: Ability to research, develop, and execute account strategies across Mid-Market segments, ideally leveraging the MEDDICC sales methodology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consultative, Value-Based Selling:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with a consultative and value-based selling approach, focused on solving business challenges and driving ROI—rather than leading with features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Communication &amp;amp; Presentation Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled at delivering compelling presentations and facilitating executive-level conversations in both remote and in-person settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience working effectively with Solutions Engineering, Account Management, Partnerships, and other go-to-market teams to drive customer success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel Readiness:&lt;/strong&gt; Willingness to travel periodically (10–15%) for customer meetings, conferences, and internal team events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role is different:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Because direct mail is a physical good, there’s a lot more stability in this opportunity as opposed to other standard SaaS opportunities. (uniquely positioned with a physical product)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lob is profitable! Tremendous total addressable market and strong product-market fit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation Information:&lt;br&gt;The compensation for this role is comprised of an annual base salary, variable compensation, and RSUs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Annual Base Salary: $71,000 - $84,750&lt;br&gt;Variable Salary: $71,000 - $84,750&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: white;&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;#LI-REMOTE #LI-RW1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;“Lob’s salary ranges are based on market data, relative to our size, industry and stage of growth. Salary is one part of total compensation, which also includes equity, perks and competitive benefits. Salary decisions are based on many factors including geographic location, qualifications for the role, skillset, proficiency and experience level. Lob reasonably expects to pay candidates who are offered roles within the provided salary ranges.”&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;We offer remote working opportunities in AZ, CA, CO, DC, FL, GA, IA, IL, MA, MD, MI, MN, MT, NE, NC, NH, NJ, NV, NY, OH, OR, PA, RI, TN, TX, UT, and WA,&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;unless specified otherwise in the job description above.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;If you are looking for a progressive, fun-spirited, and mentally stimulating environment, come join us at Lob!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;Lob is an equal opportunity employer and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot; href=&quot;https://www.lob.com/blog/power-diversity-starts-data&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;values diversity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt; of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot; href=&quot;https://www.lob.com/blog/a-commitment-to-diversity&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;backgrounds and perspectives&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt; to cultivate an environment of understanding to have greater impact on our business and customers. We encourage under-represented groups to apply and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or criminal history in accordance with local, state, and/or federal laws, including the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot; href=&quot;https://sfgov.org/olse/sites/default/files/Document/FCO%20Art.%2049%20Official%20Notice%20to%20print%202017.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;San Francisco’s Fair Chance Ordinance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recent awards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://keep.google.com/u/0/media/v2/1e8T9oEtvbqRcrMcmtMSXLguNCPTDvK9fgYyRHPMut1prD3B1tXfjRFr3o2O1dlQ/1mas8D_M3MtQ6MJEDfG-6yRUXNoeICQQ-q7BzV0N3BOFVMtPtiGQm3VTYWAtzlnE?sz=512&amp;amp;accept=image%2Fgif%2Cimage%2Fjpeg%2Cimage%2Fjpg%2Cimage%2Fpng%2Cimage%2Fwebp&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;NaN&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://builtin.com/awards/remote/2025/best-midsize-places-to-work&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#88 on BuiltIn&#39;s Best Remote Midsize Companies to Work For in 2025&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;BuiltIn Best Remote Midsize Companies to Work For in 2024&lt;br&gt;BuiltIn Best Midsize Companies to Work For 2022&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lob was founded in 2013 by technical co-founders with a vision to connect the world one mailbox at a time. Today, we&#39;re transforming the way businesses use direct mail and bringing the power of technology to a traditionally manual channel.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our modern logistics and fulfillment engine helps businesses to build and scale high-quality, personalized direct mail programs without the operational burden. As we grow to meet the evolving needs of our customers and expand our product offerings, we’re building a team to shape the future of direct mail.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is the senior technical security role at Lob and the first hire in a newly split security function. You will own the engineering side of security: cloud infrastructure, detection and response, application security, and incident response. A dedicated GRC counterpart owns audit, compliance, and customer trust, so you are not the questionnaire desk. You will partner with them, not absorb them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report directly to the CTO, manage our application security contractor, and work day to day with our Platform, Logistics, and IT teams. This is a builder role with real autonomy and a mandate to raise the security floor of a system that processes hundreds of requests per second and moves millions of physical mailpieces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you will own&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud infrastructure security&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security posture of our AWS environment, including our CNAPP program and cloud misconfiguration risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security review of infrastructure changes across Terraform, Nomad, and our Cloudflare edge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;WAF strategy and tuning at the domain level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with Platform engineers so security is designed in rather than reviewed at the end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Detection and response&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own our detection engineering practice on our SIEM, moving us from noisy alert channels to curated, high signal detections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define alert triage ownership, runbooks, and severity criteria&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own security incident response: escalation paths, tabletop exercises, post incident reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with IT on endpoint detection and endpoint vulnerability coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application and product security&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the vulnerability management program across SCA, SAST, DAST, and container scanning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and mentor our application security contractor, and route remediation work into engineering teams effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Threat modeling and security architecture review for new products and major changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve secure SDLC practice in a high velocity, AI-assisted engineering org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Penetration testing and assurance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical ownership of our annual independent penetration test: scoping, findings triage, remediation routing, retest coordination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce the technical evidence our GRC counterpart needs for SOC 2, HIPAA, and Microsoft SSPA, without owning the audit itself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security engineering and automation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tooling and automation rather than process and spreadsheets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply AI to security operations where it creates real leverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8 or more years in security engineering, with meaningful depth in cloud security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on expertise with AWS security services, IAM design, and infrastructure as code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated detection engineering experience: you have written detections, tuned them, and cut false positive rates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real incident response experience as a responder or lead, not just as a plan author&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in application security sufficient to review findings, judge severity, and argue exploitability with engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of shipping security improvements through other teams by earning trust rather than filing tickets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort as the senior technical security voice in an organization without a large security team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting SOC 2 Type 2, HIPAA, or Microsoft SSPA from the engineering side&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Container and orchestration security, particularly Nomad or Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloudflare, including Zero Trust and WAF&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a company handling regulated or consumer-identifiable data at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience mentoring or managing engineers or contractors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What this role is not&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want to be direct about scope, because we have deliberately designed this role to be technical.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will not be the primary owner of security questionnaires, RFPs, or Trust Center requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will not own the auditor relationship or the compliance calendar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will not be the sole owner of vendor security reviews or policy authoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Those live with our GRC lead. You will contribute technical input and evidence. You will not run the program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;First 90 days&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;30 days:&lt;/strong&gt; own alert triage and incident escalation, know our AWS and edge posture, take over the penetration test findings workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;60 days:&lt;/strong&gt; a working detection engineering backlog, endpoint and cloud vulnerability coverage verified end to end, application security contractor&#39;s work routed cleanly into engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;90 days:&lt;/strong&gt; a prioritized security engineering roadmap you own and defend, with the top three infrastructure risks either closed or explicitly accepted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why this role is interesting&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Physical mail is an unusual attack surface. Our security work spans a cloud platform, a print and logistics network, recipient identifiable data, and enterprise customers in regulated industries. You get executive access, a clean mandate, and a function you are helping design rather than inherit.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation Information&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The total compensation package for this role is comprised of an annual base salary and RSUs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Annual base salary: $197,500 - $220,000 base&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: white;&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;#LI-REMOTE #LI-GD1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;“Lob’s salary ranges are based on market data, relative to our size, industry and stage of growth. Salary is one part of total compensation, which also includes equity, perks and competitive benefits. Salary decisions are based on many factors including geographic location, qualifications for the role, skillset, proficiency and experience level. Lob reasonably expects to pay candidates who are offered roles within the provided salary ranges.”&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;We offer remote working opportunities in AZ, CA, CO, DC, FL, GA, IA, IL, MA, MD, MI, MN, MT, NE, NC, NH, NJ, NV, NY, OH, OR, PA, RI, TN, TX, UT, and WA,&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;unless specified otherwise in the job description above.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;If you are looking for a progressive, fun-spirited, and mentally stimulating environment, come join us at Lob!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;Lob is an equal opportunity employer and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot; href=&quot;https://www.lob.com/blog/power-diversity-starts-data&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;values diversity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt; of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot; href=&quot;https://www.lob.com/blog/a-commitment-to-diversity&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;backgrounds and perspectives&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt; to cultivate an environment of understanding to have greater impact on our business and customers. We encourage under-represented groups to apply and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or criminal history in accordance with local, state, and/or federal laws, including the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot; href=&quot;https://sfgov.org/olse/sites/default/files/Document/FCO%20Art.%2049%20Official%20Notice%20to%20print%202017.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;San Francisco’s Fair Chance Ordinance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recent awards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;max-width: 100%;&quot; src=&quot;https://keep.google.com/u/0/media/v2/1e8T9oEtvbqRcrMcmtMSXLguNCPTDvK9fgYyRHPMut1prD3B1tXfjRFr3o2O1dlQ/1mas8D_M3MtQ6MJEDfG-6yRUXNoeICQQ-q7BzV0N3BOFVMtPtiGQm3VTYWAtzlnE?sz=512&amp;amp;accept=image%2Fgif%2Cimage%2Fjpeg%2Cimage%2Fjpg%2Cimage%2Fpng%2Cimage%2Fwebp&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; width=&quot;NaN&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://builtin.com/awards/remote/2025/best-midsize-places-to-work&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;#88 on BuiltIn&#39;s Best Remote Midsize Companies to Work For in 2025&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;BuiltIn Best Remote Midsize Companies to Work For in 2024&lt;br&gt;BuiltIn Best Midsize Companies to Work For 2022&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lob was founded in 2013 by technical co-founders with a vision to connect the world one mailbox at a time. Today, we&#39;re transforming the way businesses use direct mail and bringing the power of technology to a traditionally manual channel.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our modern logistics and fulfillment engine helps businesses to build and scale high-quality, personalized direct mail programs without the operational burden. As we grow to meet the evolving needs of our customers and expand our product offerings, we’re building a team to shape the future of direct mail.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Implementation Manager, Lob Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lob Logistics is looking for a Technical Implementation Manager to lead the technical onboarding and integration of new customers and logistics partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own customer integrations from verbal commitment through launch and the first 30 days in production. You will work directly with customer technical, operational, and postal teams to understand their workflows, design the integration, configure APIs and customer profiles, troubleshoot issues, coordinate postal requirements, and ensure the solution works successfully in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lob Logistics is intentionally built around a &lt;strong&gt;white-glove customer experience&lt;/strong&gt;. Our customers are often integrating complex technology, production, postal, and logistics workflows, and we believe the best implementations require more than handing customers documentation and asking them to integrate themselves. The Technical Implementation Manager will work closely with customers throughout the process, including traveling onsite when appropriate for project scoping, technical working sessions, testing, and finalizing integrations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on technical role. You should be comfortable working with APIs, data, developer tools, and AI coding tools such as Claude Code. We are looking for someone who can solve technical problems directly rather than simply coordinate work between customers and Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right person will be equally comfortable sitting with a customer’s engineering team to design an integration, troubleshooting an API or data issue, working with a commingling partner on postal requirements, and walking a customer through the final steps required to successfully launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Customer Implementations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own new Lob Logistics customer implementations from verbal commitment through the first 30 days in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical discovery and scoping with customers, including understanding their existing systems, mail workflows, data requirements, production needs, postage strategy, billing and integration architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to customer locations as appropriate to lead project scoping, technical working sessions, implementation planning, testing, and final integration activities.&amp;nbsp; This role will have regular, consistent travel.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and document the technical implementation plan and define requirements, dependencies, testing criteria, and launch readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure customer profiles and integrations across Lob Logistics systems working with commingle partners on integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own testing, UAT, go-live, and the first 30 days of production stabilization before transitioning the customer to the long-term account owner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a high-touch, white-glove approach throughout implementation, ensuring customers have a clear technical owner who remains accountable from initial scoping through a successful production launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build &amp;amp; Troubleshoot Integrations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with customers to integrate with Lob Logistics through our APIs or customer portal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand and troubleshoot API requests, JSON payloads, authentication, webhooks, data mappings, and integration errors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Claude Code and other development tools to navigate code, investigate issues, build scripts and utilities, create working examples, and accelerate customer integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify whether technical issues originate with the customer, Lob, a partner, data, configuration, or the underlying integration and drive them to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Look for opportunities to automate repetitive implementation work and build tools that make future integrations faster and more reliable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scope Technical Solutions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determine when customer requirements can be solved through configuration or existing capabilities and when custom development is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope custom technical requirements and partner with Product and Engineering on solutions requiring platform changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear requirements, acceptance criteria, and technical context to Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the implementation project manager to ensure technical requirements, dependencies, risks, and timelines are reflected in the broader implementation plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Postal &amp;amp; Partner Setup&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate the technical and operational requirements necessary to successfully move customer mail through Lob Logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure customer implementations meet USPS and commingling requirements, including PAFs, postal promotions, customer profiles, mail owner and mail service provider configurations, and other applicable requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with Lob’s commingling partners on new customer setup and ensure all technical, operational, and postal requirements are completed before launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal postal subject matter experts when deeper expertise is required while maintaining ownership of the overall implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the customer’s technical integration works across the entire physical mail workflow, not simply at the point of API acceptance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in solutions consulting, technical consulting, implementation strategy, solutions architecture, customer success, or a similar customer-facing role working with technology and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of how business systems, applications, and data integrations work together, with familiarity with concepts such as APIs, data flows, authentication, and system integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in direct mail, print manufacturing, logistics, fulfillment, shipping, payments, EDI, or another environment where software connects to complex physical operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of USPS mail preparation, Intelligent Mail barcodes, PostalOne!, Mail.dat/Mail.XML, PAF requirements, postal promotions, commingling, drop shipping, or destination entry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with customers to understand their existing technology landscape, identify requirements, and recommend practical solution approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate ambiguous customer needs and business processes into clear technical requirements, solution designs, and implementation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable partnering with customer engineers, IT teams, and internal technical resources to guide integrations and troubleshoot implementation challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify potential technical risks, dependencies, and gaps and coordinate with the appropriate engineering or technical teams to resolve them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with modern technical tools and AI-assisted development tools is a plus, with the ability to use them to investigate questions, validate approaches, and collaborate effectively with technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to translate between technical, operational, and business audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead technical discovery and solution conversations while maintaining a strong understanding of the customer&#39;s business goals and desired outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple complex implementations while maintaining clear ownership and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong customer orientation and willingness to do what is necessary to deliver a high-touch, white-glove implementation experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias toward solving problems directly rather than simply escalating them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to travel to customer and partner locations for project scoping, technical working sessions, integration testing, and launch support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You become the clear technical owner for every implementation assigned to you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customers move from verbal commitment to production quickly and predictably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customers feel like Lob is working alongside them throughout the implementation rather than handing them an integration and waiting for it to be completed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical, postal, and operational requirements are identified early rather than becoming launch-day surprises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customers successfully operate in production during their first 30 days and transition cleanly to their long-term account owner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Routine integration challenges are solved by the Technical Implementation team without unnecessary dependency on Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer and partner integrations become more standardized, automated, and repeatable over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You develop trusted relationships with customer technical and operational teams because you understand both their systems and how their mail physically moves through the Lob Logistics network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Most importantly, you don’t just manage implementations. You make them happen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
